  "title": "AvalonEdit Region Editor \u0026 Language Picker",
  "branch": "feature/avalonedit-region-editor",
  "summary": "Replace the plain TextBox in SquadDash\u0027s inline embedded code-region editor with AvalonEdit, make the region\u0027s language label a clickable picker, and add theme-aware syntax highlighting for built-in plus bundled custom grammars. Each stage must leave the prompt editor fully usable, re-prove the native selection/copy/arrow-navigation behavior stabilized in commit 811809a0, and gate every human-observable outcome (selection, caret, copy/paste, popup placement, live highlighting, light/dark color correctness) behind a human approval checkpoint. Keep the editor host reusable and the highlighting palette pluggable for a future Markdown-editing reuse, but add no v2 tasks.",
  "tasks": [
    {
      "taskId": "AVALONEDIT-20261014-001",
      "title": "Define AvalonEdit integration and theming strategy",
      "description": "Produce the architecture decision that lets Lyra migrate the embedded code-region editor safely, without making this task the feature implementer.\n\n## Observable outcome\n\nA concise written strategy (committed where the team keeps architecture notes) that the migration task consumes, covering: how AvalonEdit\u0027s TextEditor replaces the BlockUIContainer-hosted TextBox in EmbeddedCodeRegionBlock; how native caret/mouse selection, the custom Ctrl\u002BC/Ctrl\u002BX fenced copy, and Up/Down arrow boundary-exit navigation re-map from TextBox APIs onto AvalonEdit TextArea/Caret/Document; and how light/dark HighlightingColor palettes are pushed into the editor on each theme switch, given AvalonEdit colors are not WPF DynamicResource-driven.\n\n## Constraints\n\nAvalonEdit colors must be re-applied through a new per-editor hook invoked from MainWindow.ApplyTheme / NotifyThemeChanged rather than relying on SetResourceReference. Keep the editor host and the palette source pluggable so a future Markdown-highlighting reuse is not foreclosed, but do not design or schedule that v2 work.\n\n## Consumers\n\nTasks 002 and 004 consume this strategy as their integration and theming contract.",
