    {
      "taskId": "AVALONEDIT-20261014-002",
      "title": "Replace region TextBox with AvalonEdit editor",
      "description": "Stage 1. Replace the plain Consolas TextBox inside EmbeddedCodeRegionBlock with AvalonEdit\u0027s TextEditor, introducing the new \u0060ICSharpCode.AvalonEdit\u0060 NuGet dependency (first use in the solution), and re-plumb every region behavior currently wired against TextBox APIs. No syntax colors in this stage.\n\n## Observable outcome\n\nTyping three backticks in the prompt RichTextBox still creates an embedded code region, now backed by AvalonEdit, with: working single-click caret placement and caret movement; double-click word selection; click-drag range selection; double-click-drag word-wise extension; the custom Ctrl\u002BC / Ctrl\u002BX fenced copy/cut; Up/Down arrow boundary-exit navigation that leaves the region; TextChanged to Content sync; focus routing into and out of the region; and theme-following background/foreground via the strategy\u0027s palette hook (plain editor colors only). The re-plumbed selection gesture must preserve the behavior stabilized in commit 811809a0, including the pure claim predicate (currently ShouldClaimRegionMouseGesture) and the bubbling-stage host-selection collapse in both EmbeddedCodeRegionBlock and MainWindow.PromptTextBox_PreviewMouseLeftButtonDown.\n\n## Serialization\n\nLand the fence serialization convention here: an explicit language serializes as a three-backtick fence followed by the language token; Auto detect serializes as a bare three-backtick fence with no language token; Plain text serializes with the reserved token text. Round-tripping a region must preserve its mode.\n\n## Consumers\n\nThe production prompt editor consumes the migrated control. Tasks 003 and 004 build the picker and highlighting on this host; task 007 adds headless regression coverage.",
      "dependsOn": [
        "AVALONEDIT-20261014-001"
      ],
