    {
      "taskId": "AVALONEDIT-20261014-004",
      "title": "Highlight built-in grammars with theme-aware palettes",
      "description": "Stage 3. Apply automatic syntax highlighting for AvalonEdit\u0027s standard built-in grammars, with distinct light and dark HighlightingColor palettes, and implement the Auto-detect content heuristic.\n\n## Observable outcome\n\nWhen a region\u0027s mode resolves to a built-in grammar, the editor renders syntax colors. A new per-editor theme hook, invoked from MainWindow.ApplyTheme via NotifyThemeChanged, re-pushes the correct light or dark HighlightingColor palette into every open region editor on each theme switch (AvalonEdit colors are not DynamicResource-driven). Auto-detect resolves the grammar from the fence tag first; when the fence tag is empty it runs a debounced content heuristic after text changes, so while the region is in Auto-detect mode the applied highlighting updates live as the user types. When the user picks Plain text or any explicit language tag, the mode is pinned and the heuristic does not run on further changes.\n\n## Constraints\n\nKeep the palette source pluggable (a future Markdown scheme must be able to register without reworking this engine). Preserve the Stage 1 selection, copy, navigation, and sync behavior.\n\n## Consumers\n\nThe production region editor consumes the highlighting engine, theme hook, and auto-detect engine. Tasks 005 and 006 register custom grammars and palettes through the same engine and hook; task 008 covers the heuristic and pinning logic headlessly.",
      "dependsOn": [
        "AVALONEDIT-20261014-003"
      ],
      "priority": "high",
      "status": "pending",
      "agentAssignments": [
        {
          "agentHandle": "lyra-morn",
          "role": "Implement built-in-grammar highlighting, theme palette hook, and auto-detect heuristic",
          "allowGenericChildren": true
        }
      ],
      "agentRoutingMode": "assigned",
      "outputs": [
        {
          "outputId": "highlighting-engine",
          "description": "Pluggable AvalonEdit highlighting application that maps a resolved region grammar to active HighlightingDefinition and colors."
        },
        {
          "outputId": "theme-palette-hook",
          "description": "Per-editor light/dark HighlightingColor palette re-application invoked from MainWindow.ApplyTheme via NotifyThemeChanged on each theme switch."
        },
        {
          "outputId": "auto-detect-engine",
          "description": "Fence-tag-first grammar resolution with a debounced live content heuristic for empty tags, pinned off when Plain text or an explicit language is chosen."
        }
      ],
      "inputs": [
        "avalonedit-region-host",
        "language-picker-mode"
      ],
