    {
      "taskId": "AVALONEDIT-20261014-008",
      "title": "Regression coverage for picker and auto-detect logic",
      "description": "Add focused headless NUnit coverage in SquadDash.Tests for the deterministic logic behind the language picker write-through and the auto-detect engine.\n\n## Observable outcome\n\nNew or updated tests pass covering: picker selection writing the correct fence tag for each mode and persisting across a serialization round-trip; auto-detect resolving the grammar from the fence tag first; auto-detect falling back to the content heuristic only when the fence tag is empty; and the heuristic being pinned off (not re-running on text changes) once Plain text or an explicit language is selected. Tests run via the existing \u0060dotnet test\u0060 path for SquadDash.Tests.\n\n## Consumers\n\nThese tests back the Stage 2 and Stage 3 human gates with automated proof of the non-visual logic, letting the gates focus on strictly human-observable rendering.",
      "dependsOn": [
        "AVALONEDIT-20261014-004"
      ],
      "priority": "mid",
      "status": "pending",
      "agentAssignments": [
        {
          "agentHandle": "vesper-knox",
          "role": "Author headless regression tests for picker write-through and auto-detect resolution/pinning",
          "allowGenericChildren": true
        }
      ],
      "parallelEligible": true,
      "agentRoutingMode": "assigned",
      "outputs": [
        {
          "outputId": "picker-autodetect-regression-suite",
          "description": "Headless coverage of picker fence write-through persistence and auto-detect fence-first resolution, empty-tag heuristic fallback, and pinned-off behavior."
        }
      ],
      "inputs": [
        "language-picker-mode",
        "auto-detect-engine"
      ],
      "proofRequirements": [
        {
          "requirementId": "picker-autodetect-tests",
          "proofType": "automated-test",
          "description": "Run the new SquadDash.Tests cases covering picker write-through persistence and auto-detect resolution and pinning, and report pass counts."
        }
      ],
      "displayStepLabel": "7",
      "executionMode": "implementation"
    },
    {
      "taskId": "AVALONEDIT-20261014-006",
      "title": "Bundle custom grammars: Go, Rust, Bash, Markdown",
      "description": "Stage 5. Add and bundle custom AvalonEdit .xshd highlighting grammars for Go, Rust, Bash, and Markdown, registered with the picker list, the highlighting engine, and the light/dark palette hook.\n\n## Observable outcome\n\nEach of Go, Rust, Bash, and Markdown appears in the language picker and, when selected or auto-detected, renders its own syntax highlighting with correct light and dark colors in a region. The grammars load from embedded resources without runtime exceptions.\n\n## Consumers\n\nThe production region editor and picker consume the four new grammars through the existing engine and hook. The following human validation gate uses copy-ready sample snippets to confirm per-language color correctness and allows iterative palette tuning. Keep the Markdown grammar registration path reusable, but add no further v2 Markdown-editor work.",
      "dependsOn": [
        "AVALONEDIT-20261014-005"
      ],
      "priority": "mid",
      "status": "pending",
      "agentAssignments": [
        {
          "agentHandle": "lyra-morn",
